       While these functions are intended to be used to support a signal  han‐
       dler  (i.e., for SSIIGGWWIINNCCHH), care should be taken to avoid invoking them
       in a context where mmaalllloocc or rreeaalllloocc may have been  interrupted,  since
       it uses those functions.

       If _n_c_u_r_s_e_s is configured to supply its own SSIIGGWWIINNCCHH handler,

       •   on receipt of a SSIIGGWWIINNCCHH, the handler sets a flag

       •   which is tested in wwggeettcchh(3X), ddoouuppddaattee(3X) and rreessttaarrtttteerrmm(3X),

       •   in turn, calling the rreessiizzeetteerrmm function,

       •   which uunnggeettcchh's a KKEEYY__RREESSIIZZEE which will be read on the next call to
           wwggeettcchh.

           The KKEEYY__RREESSIIZZEE alerts an  application  that  the  screen  size  has
           changed,  and  that it should repaint special features such as pads
